  "id": "COMPOUND:18105 - PROTEIN:4915",
  "verbalization": "Interiorin appears to have a direct relationship with Replicase polyprotein 1ab through a series of intermediate targets, all of which are involved in the mitochondrial thioredoxin pathway. The evidence suggests that Interiorin targets Thioredoxin, a protein that is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including Diplotrin A and 5-Hydroxy-2-Methylchromone-7-O-Rutinoside. These compounds, in turn, have a shared target of Replicase polyprotein 1ab. This chain of interactions implies that Interiorin may influence the function of Replicase polyprotein 1ab through the mitochondrial thioredoxin pathway, potentially by modulating the activity of the intermediates involved. The presence of multiple targets in this pathway supports the idea that Interiorin's effects are mediated through a complex network of molecular interactions, with Replicase polyprotein 1ab being a downstream effector. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of thioredoxin in the biological processes that Interiorin may regulate.",
